# Registry content sync

## Why

[`shared/schema.ts`](shared/schema.ts) re-exports Zod schemas from gitignored `site_*/component-registry/**/schema.ts`. Those folders are **content-synced** (GitHub), not part of the app git repo. If the app PR adds a named re-export before local/remote content has that export, `npm run dev` / `npm run build` crash at module load — before the Sync UI or startup auto-pull can run.

Site-only components must keep schemas under `site_*` (do not move everything into tracked `marketing-content`).

## Landing a new variant / export

1. Add or update `schema.ts` in the **content** repo under `site_<name>/component-registry/<type>/vX.Y/`.
2. Pull content locally: `npm run content:pull` (or GitHub Sync once the server is up).
3. Then land the app change that re-exports from `shared/schema.ts`.

Never ship a new `shared/schema.ts` re-export alone.

## Boot-critical imports

Prefer not adding new top-level re-exports in `shared/schema.ts` for purely site-only variants unless a shared union/type truly needs them. Prefer per-site registry loading when possible so one missing site-only export does not brick every boot.

## Commands

| Script | Role |
|--------|------|
| `npm run check:registry` | Import `shared/schema`; fail with recovery steps |
| `npm run content:pull` | Hash-diff pull all sites (`--force` for full) |
| `npm run ensure:registry` | Check → pull on failure → re-check (used by `predev` / `prebuild`) |

`content:pull` needs `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `github_repo_url` in `sites.yml`. It does **not** require `GITHUB_SYNC_ENABLED`.
